STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Improving sleep health in post-secondary students: Evidence-based coping strategies and knowledge translation tools
LOCATION:Amphitheatre\, 4333 Côte-Ste-Catherine Rd.\, Montreal QC H3T 1E4
CATEGORIES:Psychosocial Research Rounds
DESCRIPTION:Psychosocial Research Rounds\n\nTOPIC: Improving sleep health in post-secondary students: Evidence-based coping strategies and knowledge translation tools\n\nSPEAKER: Noemi Di Pietrantonio\n\nLEARNING OBJECTIVES:\n• To synthesize the current evidence on interventions for common parasomnias and sleep-related disorders and translate this evidence into accessible\, evidence-informed resources for young adults and healthcare professionals.\n• To bridge the gap between research evidence and practical sleep health resources for post-secondary students.\n• To identify evidence-based behavioural\, psychological\, pharmacological\, and educational interventions for common parasomnias.\n\nMEETING LINK: https://us06web.zoom.us/j/88488947071?pwd=SfbahYa0VEe7nCL2Hbc1aA6bXzfZeR.1\n\nORGANIZER: Vincent Paquin
