STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Connected beginnings: How adult attachment style shapes perinatal mental health and early parental functioning
LOCATION:Amphitheatre\, 4333 Côte-Ste-Catherine Rd.\, Montreal QC H3T 1E4
CATEGORIES:Psychosocial Research Rounds
DESCRIPTION:Psychosocial Research Rounds\n\nTOPIC: Connected beginnings: How adult attachment style shapes perinatal mental health and early parental functioning\n\nSPEAKER: Adrianne Tan\n\nLEARNING OBJECTIVES:\n• Describe how adult attachment styles are associated with vulnerability to perinatal mood and anxiety disorders (PMADs) across the perinatal period.\n• Explain how insecure adult attachment and PMAD symptoms may contribute to early parenting outcomes\, including parental functioning\, self-efficacy\, caregiving sensitivity\, and parent-infant bonding.\n• Reflect on the implications of adult attachment and PMAD symptoms for supporting parent-infant relationships and informing attachment-focused prevention and intervention strategies.\n\nMEETING LINK: https://us06web.zoom.us/j/88488947071?pwd=SfbahYa0VEe7nCL2Hbc1aA6bXzfZeR.1\n\nORGANIZER: Vincent Paquin
